From 9b0d927f4e63f2ab971532c4395adb44f8d683aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MendixMau <mauritscgvisser@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 10:43:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pages): ALTER PAGE/SNIPPET SET RenderMode on a dynamic
 text (closes #1228)

`alter page P { set RenderMode = H2 on <dynamictext> }` was refused as "not a
property of this built-in widget", although CREATE PAGE and REPLACE accept
RenderMode on a dynamictext and the MCP backend's mutator already sets it.
setRawWidgetPropertyMut had no case for it, so it fell through to the
pluggable-property setter.

Add a RenderMode case dispatched on the stored $Type (Forms$DynamicText): the
value is validated case-insensitively against Text, Paragraph and H1-H6 and
written in its canonical spelling; anything else is refused with the accepted
list, leaving the document untouched. Other widgets keep the previous path.
`check -p` picks this up too, since it dry-runs the same setter.

Docs: alter-page skill, docs-site alter-page.md, MDL_QUICK_REFERENCE.md,
`mxcli syntax page.alter`, and a fix-issue finding.

Tested: make test (84 packages ok, 0 FAIL), make lint. The new unit tests fail
without the mutator change (8 subtests) and pass with it.
Mendix 11.12.2, fresh blank app: the bug-test script exits 1 on main and
applies on this branch (describe: H2, Paragraph, H4); mx check 0 errors; H7
refused with nothing written; at runtime the home-page heading set to H5
renders as <h5>.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
